// Sample headless-onboarding answers for the ICM tree.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// PUBLIC VISIBILITY — READ BEFORE PASTING ANYTHING REAL IN HERE.
//
// This repository is the `kozure/icm-metaharness` fork and it is PUBLIC, and it
// inherits upstream `ruvnet/metaharness`'s public visibility. Everything in this
// file is world-readable forever, including history.
//
// So this file carries STRUCTURAL / PLACEHOLDER VALUES ONLY. Never put personal
// context, credentials, tokens, API keys, machine paths, internal hostnames, or
// real brand data in it. If you need a filled-in config for a real project, put
// it outside the repository — pass its path to `--answers` and keep it in your
// own tree (or a secret store). The generator only ever *reads* the path you
// give it; it never copies the file into the harness.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Format (task 4.1): a JSON object keyed by ICM question id, which is the
// `{{SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE}}` placeholder or `{{?CONDITIONAL}}` section name the
// emitted tree actually contains. The set is derived from the ICM content, not
// hand-listed — and the same set is what `templates/catalog.json` publishes as
// `icm.questions` for a template, so `--list`-style tooling and the generator
// cannot disagree about what a question is called.
//
// `//` full-line comments like these are allowed (a data line can never start
// with `//` in JSON); trailing comments are not.
//
// Keys are ALL REQUIRED in headless mode. There are no implicit defaults: an
// omitted key is reported by name with its `file:line` and the run exits
// non-zero (task 4.7). That is deliberate — a generator that silently invents
// `npm test` for you is the silent gap this feature exists to prevent.
//
// For `vertical:coding` the full set is the six questions below. Text questions
// take a non-empty string; `{{?NAME}}` conditionals take a boolean, where `true`
// keeps the section and `false` removes it including its heading.

{
  // Stage 01 (plan) — the scope boundary every later stage reads.
  "PROJECT_GOAL": "Describe this harness's project goal in one sentence",

  // Stage 02 (implement) — how the project is built or compiled.
  "BUILD_COMMAND": "npm run build",

  // Stage 03 (test) — how the suite is run.
  "TEST_COMMAND": "npm test",

  // Stage 04 (review) — what a review must focus on.
  "REVIEW_FOCUS": "Correctness, security, and reuse",

  // Stage 01 (plan) — `{{?SUBAGENT_HANDOFF}}`: hand the plan to a subagent.
  "SUBAGENT_HANDOFF": true,

  // Stage 03 (test) — `{{?FIX_LOOP}}`: keep the failing-test fix loop.
  "FIX_LOOP": true
}
